==Special attack==
[[File:Soul Rend.gif|thumb|250px|A player using the Eye of Ayak's special attack, ''Soul Rend''.]]
The Eye of Ayak has a [[special attack]], ''Soul Rend'', which consumes 50% of the player's special attack energy. It has an attack speed of five ticks, compared to the staff's standard attack speed of three ticks, but has double the accuracy and a 30% higher maximum hit.

If the attack deals damage, it reduces the target's Magic Defence by an amount equal to the damage dealt. This differs from the [[accursed sceptre]], which drains the target's Magic level. As Magic Defence is not a stat, NPCs cannot restore it, and the reduction remains until the target is killed or despawns.

Although Magic Defence cannot be reduced below 0, the full reduction persists if the target's Magic Defence subsequently changes. For example, if the special attack deals 50 damage to [[Yama]] while he is in his melee stance, which has −30 Magic Defence, his Magic Defence remains at -30. If he then changes to his magic stance, his actual Magic Defence becomes +10 during phases 1 and 2, or +31 during phase 3, rather than +60 or +81 respectively. This also applies to [[Zulrah]], whose tanzanite form has Magic Defence while its serpentine and magma forms do not.

==Charging==
To use the staff's built-in spell, it must either be charged with [[demon tears]] or with both [[death rune|death]] and [[chaos rune]]s. It can hold up to 50,000 charges, enough for 25 hours of continuous combat. Each cast consumes either one demon tear, or two death runes and one chaos rune, depending on what the staff is charged with. Using demon tears costs {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Demon tear|1}}|c}} per charge, while using runes costs {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Death rune|2}}+{{GEP|Chaos rune|1}}|c}} per charge. The eye cannot contain both demon tear charges and rune-based charges at the same time.

Any remaining charges can be removed using the 'Uncharge' option, returning all demon tears or runes used to charge it. 

